  "body": [
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "Vidyāsthānopamasūtra",
      "segment_number": 1,
      "translated_text": "<s>Vidyāsthānopamasūtra</s> (The Sūtra of the Simile of the Fields of Knowledge)"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "1 evaṃ may",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ā śru",
          "segment_number": 3,
          "translated_text": "hea-"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "tam / ekasmiṃ samaye bhagavāṃ śrāvastyāṃ vi",
          "segment_number": 4,
          "translated_text": "rd. At one time the <s>Bhagavān</s> (Blessed One) was dwelling in <s>Śrāvastī</s>,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "harati sma jetava",
          "segment_number": 5,
          "translated_text": "in the <s>Jetava-</s>"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "ne anāthapiṇḍadārāme /",
          "segment_number": 6,
          "translated_text": "na, <s>Anāthapiṇḍada's</s> park."
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 2,
      "translated_text": "§1 Thus have I"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "2 tatra bhagavāṃ bhikṣūn āmaṃtrayate sma /",
      "segment_number": 7,
      "translated_text": "§2 There the <s>Bhagavān</s> addressed the <s>bhikṣus</s> (monks):"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "utpādā",
          "segment_number": 9,
          "translated_text": "\"Whether,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "d vā bhikṣavaḥ tathāgatānām anutpādād vā saṃvartate ca loko vivartate ca /",
          "segment_number": 10,
          "translated_text": "O <s>bhikṣus</s>, <s>Tathāgatas</s> arise or do not arise, the world contracts and expands."
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "different beginning for paragraphs 1-3 in Or.15009/83v; ed. in: The British Library Sanskrit Fragments, vol. II, ed. S. Karashima and K. Wille, Tokyo 2009 (Buddhist Manuscripts from Central Asia), pp. 153f.:\n1 /// .. ye bhagavāṃ śrāvastyāṃ viharati sma je[tava]ne a .. .. + + ///",
          "segment_number": 11,
          "translated_text": "[Editorial note:] Different beginning for paragraphs 1–3 in Or.15009/83v; edited in: The British Library Sanskrit Fragments, vol. II, ed. S. Karashima and K. Wille, Tokyo 2009 (Buddhist Manuscripts from Central Asia), pp. 153f.: §1 /// ...the <s>Bhagavān</s> was dwelling in <s>Śrāvastī</s>, in the <s>Jetava</s>[na]... ///"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 8,
      "translated_text": "§3"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "2 /// .. .y. dau kalyāṇaṃ madhye kalyāṇaṃ pa[rya]vasāne kaly[āṇaṃ] + ///",
          "segment_number": 12,
          "translated_text": "§2 /// ...beginning auspicious, middle auspicious, end auspicious... ///"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "3 /// + ṣyāmi yad uta vidya[sthā]nopamaṃ nāma dharmaparyāyas tac chṛnu[t]. [s]. ///",
          "segment_number": 13,
          "translated_text": "§3 /// ...I shall [teach] that which is the <s>dharmaparyāya</s> (discourse on the Dharma) called the Simile of the Fields of Knowledge; listen... ///"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "4 /// dharmaparyāya katama utpādād vā tathāgatāṇām a .. ///",
          "segment_number": 14,
          "translated_text": "§4 /// ...what is this <s>dharmaparyāya</s>? Whether <s>Tathāgatas</s> arise or... ///"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "For this wording cf. Daśottarasūtra E.a-c",
          "segment_number": 15,
          "translated_text": "[Editorial note:] For this wording cf. <s>Daśottarasūtra</s> E.a-c."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "4 saṃvartamāne loke yadbhūyasā satvā ābhasvare devanikāye upapadyante /",
      "segment_number": 16,
      "translated_text": "§4 When the world is contracting, for the most part beings are reborn in the <s>Ābhasvara</s> (Radiant) divine realm."
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "5 te tatra bhavanti rūpiṇo",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "mano",
          "segment_number": 18,
          "translated_text": "mind-"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "mayā avikalā ahīnendriyā",
          "segment_number": 19,
          "translated_text": "made, with complete faculties, with unimpaired senses,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ḥ",
          "segment_number": 20,
          "translated_text": "[continued]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "sarvāṅgapratyaṅgopetā",
          "segment_number": 21,
          "translated_text": "endowed with all major and minor limbs,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ḥ",
          "segment_number": 22,
          "translated_text": "[continued]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "śubhā varṇasthāyina",
          "segment_number": 23,
          "translated_text": "beautiful, of lasting complexion,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ḥ",
          "segment_number": 24,
          "translated_text": "[continued]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "prītibhakṣā",
          "segment_number": 25,
          "translated_text": "feeding on rapture,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ḥ",
          "segment_number": 26,
          "translated_text": "[continued]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "prītyāhārā",
          "segment_number": 27,
          "translated_text": "nourished by rapture,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ḥ",
          "segment_number": 28,
          "translated_text": "[continued]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "svayaṃprabhā vaihāyasagāmino dīrghāyuṣo dīrgham adhvānaṃ tiṣṭhaṃti /",
          "segment_number": 29,
          "translated_text": "self-luminous, moving through the sky, long-lived, abiding for a long period."
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 17,
      "translated_text": "§5 There they exist as corporeal beings,"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "6 vivartamāne loke pṛthak chilpasthānakarmasthānāni prajñāyante /",
      "segment_number": 30,
      "translated_text": "§6 When the world is expanding, various fields of craft and fields of work become known."
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {},
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "7 tadyathā",
          "segment_number": 31,
          "translated_text": "§7 Namely:"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "mantrā japā auṣadhayo māyākarma cikitsitam /",
          "segment_number": 32,
          "translated_text": "Spells, incantations, medicines, magic arts, healing,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "divyaṃ ca cakṣu ṛddhiś ca yathocitaṃ jñānadarśanam //",
          "segment_number": 33,
          "translated_text": "the divine eye, supernatural powers, and knowledge-and-vision as appropriate. //"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "8",
      "segment_number": 34,
      "translated_text": "§8"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "mārgan tu na prajānaṃti duḥkhopaśamagāminam /\nunmārge na vihanyantaś caranti amarā yathā /\nanissaraṇadarśina",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ḥ",
          "segment_number": 36,
          "translated_text": "[continued]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "//",
          "segment_number": 37,
          "translated_text": "//"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 35,
      "translated_text": "But they do not understand the path leading to the cessation of suffering; not being obstructed by the wrong path, they wander like immortals, seeing no escape"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "c: read unmārgena, s.e. for unmārgeṇa",
          "segment_number": 38,
          "translated_text": "[Editorial note:] c: read unmārgeṇa, sandhi for unmārgeṇa."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "9 yasmiṃs tu samaye tathāgatā arhantaḥ samyaksaṃbuddhā loke utpadyante yāni ca laukikāni pṛthak chilpasthānakarmasthānāni yac ca lokottaraṃ tat sarvam abhijñāya",
      "segment_number": 39,
      "translated_text": "§9 But at whatever time <s>Tathāgatas</s>, <s>Arhats</s>, fully enlightened <s>Samyaksaṃbuddhas</s>, arise in the world — having fully comprehended all the worldly fields of craft and fields of work, and also the supramundane —"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "yac chreṣṭhaṃ sarvavidyānāṃ tad deśayaṃti tathāgatāḥ /",
      "segment_number": 40,
      "translated_text": "that which is supreme among all fields of knowledge, that the <s>Tathāgatas</s> teach. /"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "10 yad uta idaṃ duḥkham āryasatyaṃ ayaṃ du",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ḥ",
          "segment_number": 42,
          "translated_text": "[continued]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "khanirodhagāminī pratipad āryasatyam i",
          "segment_number": 43,
          "translated_text": "fering, the Noble Truth of the path leading to the cessation of suf-"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ti /",
          "segment_number": 44,
          "translated_text": "fering.'"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 41,
      "translated_text": "§10 Namely: 'This is the Noble Truth of suffering (<s>duḥkham āryasatyam</s>)'; 'This is the path leading to the cessation of suf-"
    },
    {
      "tag": "l",
      "attributes": {
        "rend": "blue"
      },
      "text": "cf. Pelliot Sanskrit bleu 375rw: /// (ārya)satyaṃ ayaṃ duḥkha[s](amuday). ///",
      "segment_number": 45,
      "translated_text": "[Editorial note:] cf. Pelliot Sanskrit bleu 375rw: /// (<s>ārya</s>)satyaṃ ayaṃ duḥkha[s](amuday)... ///"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "11\ntac chreṣṭhaṃ sarvavidyānāṃ yad deśayaṃti tathāgatāḥ /\nsarvam eke prajānaṃti śramaṇabrāhmaṇā",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ḥ",
          "segment_number": 47,
          "translated_text": "[continued]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "pṛthak /",
          "segment_number": 48,
          "translated_text": "individually understand. /"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 46,
      "translated_text": "§11 That which is supreme among all fields of knowledge, which the <s>Tathāgatas</s> teach — all [of it] some <s>śramaṇas</s> (ascetics) and <s>brāhmaṇas</s>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "12\nmantrā japā auṣadhay",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "o",
          "segment_number": 50,
          "translated_text": "es,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "māyākarma cikitsi",
          "segment_number": 51,
          "translated_text": "magic arts, heal-"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "taṃ /\ndivyaṃ",
          "segment_number": 52,
          "translated_text": "ing,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "ca cakṣu ṛddhiś ca uditaṃ jñ",
          "segment_number": 53,
          "translated_text": "the divine"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ānadarśa",
          "segment_number": 54,
          "translated_text": "eye, supernatural powers, and the arisen knowledge-and-vi-"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "nam /",
          "segment_number": 55,
          "translated_text": "sion. /"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "d: cf. Pelliot Sanskrit bleu 375ry: /// ṛddhiś ca uditaṃ jñānada ///",
          "segment_number": 56,
          "translated_text": "[Editorial note:] d: cf. Pelliot Sanskrit bleu 375ry: /// ṛddhiś ca uditaṃ jñānada ///"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 49,
      "translated_text": "§12 Spells, incantations, medicin-"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "13\nmārgaṃ tu na prajānaṃti duḥkhopaśamagāminam /\nte mārgam aprajānanto duḥkhop",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "aśa",
              "segment_number": 58,
              "translated_text": "fer-"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "ma",
              "segment_number": 59,
              "translated_text": "ing"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "gāminam /\nunmā",
              "segment_number": 60,
              "translated_text": "leading to the cessation,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "rge",
              "segment_number": 61,
              "translated_text": "by the wrong"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "na vihanya",
              "segment_number": 62,
              "translated_text": "path"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "n",
              "segment_number": 63,
              "translated_text": "[continued]"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "t",
              "segment_number": 64,
              "translated_text": "not"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "aś ca",
              "segment_number": 65,
              "translated_text": "being obstructed, wan-"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "ranti amarā",
              "segment_number": 66,
              "translated_text": "der like immortals,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "yathā /",
              "segment_number": 67,
              "translated_text": "[continued]"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "anissa",
              "segment_number": 68,
              "translated_text": "seeing no esc-"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "raṇadarśina",
              "segment_number": 69,
              "translated_text": "ape,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "ḥ",
              "segment_number": 70,
              "translated_text": "[continued]"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 71,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 57,
          "translated_text": "§13 But they do not understand the path leading to the cessation of suffering; they, not understanding the path leading to the cessation of suf-"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "e: cf. Pelliot Sanskrit bleu 375rz: /// .. vihanyaś caranti amarā ///; read",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "unmā",
              "segment_number": 73,
              "translated_text": "unmā-"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "rge",
              "segment_number": 74,
              "translated_text": "rge-"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "ṇa",
              "segment_number": 75,
              "translated_text": "ṇa [i.e., unmārgeṇa, 'by the wrong path']."
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 72,
          "translated_text": "[Editorial note:] e: cf. Pelliot Sanskrit bleu 375rz: /// ...vihanyaś caranti amarā ///; read"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "14\nyadā tu loke saṃbuddhā",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "utpadyante karu",
          "segment_number": 77,
          "translated_text": "compassionate ones, arise,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "ṇikāḥ /\nprakāśayaṃti sa",
          "segment_number": 78,
          "translated_text": "they illuminate the true"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "ddha",
          "segment_number": 79,
          "translated_text": "<s>Dha-</s>"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "rmaṃ sarvaduḥkhavinodanam //",
          "segment_number": 80,
          "translated_text": "rma, the dispeller of all suffering. //"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 76,
      "translated_text": "§14 But when in the world fully enlightened <s>Buddhas</s>,"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "bc: cf. Pelliot Sanskrit bleu 375v1: /// + [g]ā · prakāśayaṃti ye [dh](armaṃ) ///; cf. also next paragraph",
          "segment_number": 81,
          "translated_text": "[Editorial note:] bc: cf. Pelliot Sanskrit bleu 375v1: /// ...prakāśayaṃti ye [dh](armaṃ) ///; cf. also next paragraph."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "15\nduḥkhaṃ duḥkhasamutpādaṃ duḥkha",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "sya",
          "segment_number": 83,
          "translated_text": "coming"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "samatikramaṃ /\nāry",
          "segment_number": 84,
          "translated_text": "of suffering,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "aṃ cāṣṭāṅgi",
          "segment_number": 85,
